    "content": "Dan Hurley is the head coach of the UConn men’s basketball team, leading the Huskies since 2018. He has transformed the program into a national powerhouse, winning consecutive NCAA championships in 2023 and 2024. Known for his intense coaching style, Hurley previously led programs at Rhode Island and Wagner College. Key Details About Dan Hurley: Role: Head Coach (Men's Basketball), hired March 22, 2018. Championships: Won the 2023 and 2024 NCAA National Championships. 2023-24 Season: Guided the Huskies to a dominant top-tier offense. Coaching History: Formerly coached at the University of Rhode Island (2012–2018) and Wagner College (2010–2012). Coaching Staff (2025-26 Season): Associate Head Coach: Kimani Young Assistant Coaches: Luke Murray, Mike Nardi Note: For the women's basketball program, Geno Auriemma is the head coach. Watch this interview with Coach Dan Hurley after a 2026 win:04:03BIG EAST ConferenceYouTube• Mar 28, 2026 04:03",
